"""Survival website copy for the owner-approved paid adults-only candidate."""
from html import escape
BASE='https://tripperdeelabs.com'
LINKS='<p><a href="/survival/">Survival</a> · <a href="/survival/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/survival/support/">Support</a></p>'
PRIVACY = "SURVIVAL — PRIVACY POLICY\nEffective November 9, 2026\nApp: com.tripperdeelabs.survival\nPublisher: TripperDeeLabs • tripperdeelabs@gmail.com\n\nSurvival is a paid, offline-first reference and planning app. It has no account system, advertising, analytics SDK or in-app purchases. Google Play handles the upfront app payment under its own privacy practices; Survival does not receive payment-card details.\n\nON YOUR DEVICE\nGuides, downloaded maps, kit/pantry choices, saved waypoints and breadcrumb trails are stored in app storage. The app does not send them to a TripperDeeLabs server. No background-location permission is requested. Location tools operate while their screens are in use; permission can be revoked in Android Settings. Location estimates, compass readings and altitude may be inaccurate or unavailable.\n\nOPTIONAL ONLINE FEATURES\nBrowsing/downloading regional maps contacts the Mapsforge mirror at Hochschule Esslingen. That service receives your IP address and requested catalog/region. Android DownloadManager may continue a confirmed download after you leave the screen; Wi-Fi is selected by default, roaming is disabled, and the app offers cancellation.\nUSGS local topographic downloads send tile coordinates identifying your chosen area and your IP address to the USGS map service.\nNearby-place refresh sends coordinates to OpenStreetMap Overpass and, for U.S. coverage, FEMA to obtain nearby records. Find my region sends coordinates to the device's Android Geocoder provider. These optional operations involve precise location/selected area and third-party processing. Their operators control their own logs and retention; this app cannot delete those logs.\nSource and credit links open the external browser. Providers may receive normal connection information. No connection is needed to read bundled guides or open already-saved regional maps.\n\nCAMERA / LIGHT\nCamera permission is used only to operate the flashlight/SOS torch where hardware supports it. Survival does not record or upload photographs, video or audio.\n\nSHARING AND CALLS\nCoordinate sharing opens the Android share sheet only at your request. The recipient/app you choose receives the shared information and applies its own privacy policy. Emergency call controls open the dialer; they do not automatically place calls or contact rescuers.\n\nDELETION / CONTROLS\nDelete regional maps in Offline regions, delete saved waypoints or clear the breadcrumb trail in Navigate, and edit kit/pantry entries in the app. Android Settings > Apps > Survival > Storage > Clear storage removes local app records; uninstall also removes app storage. Cancel a running map download before clearing storage/uninstalling. No remote user account exists to delete. Android cloud app backup is disabled; platform/device-transfer behavior may depend on the OS.\n\nCONTACT AND CHANGES\nQuestions or corrections: tripperdeelabs@gmail.com. Future updates may revise this policy and its effective date. No sale of user data or targeted advertising is implemented by Survival.\n"
def build(page):
    image=BASE+'/assets/apps/survival/feature.png'
    body='<section class="catalog-hero"><img class="app-icon" src="/assets/apps/survival/icon.png" width="112" height="112" alt="Survival compass icon"><p class="eyebrow">Android · For adults 18+</p><h1>Survival</h1><p class="lead">Your offline field guide.</p><p>Prepare for the outdoors with practical reference guides, supply checklists, downloadable regional maps and field tools.</p><p><strong>Coming soon.</strong> Planned US$0.99 upfront, with no ads, subscriptions or in-app purchases. Not yet released on Google Play.</p></section><section><h2>Prepare before you leave reception</h2><ul><li>Read 102 offline chapters, search reference material and save favorites.</li><li>Plan your bug-out bag, food supplies, water and battery needs.</li><li>Choose and download regional OpenStreetMap-based maps over Wi-Fi, then view them offline.</li><li>Use a compass, available elevation estimates, saved waypoints and an on-screen breadcrumb trail.</li></ul><p>Internet is needed for downloads, optional location lookups and external source links. Maps do not provide turn-by-turn routing or live conditions. Trail recording runs while Navigate is visible.</p></section><section><h2>Inside the current Android preview</h2><p>Actual app-window captures from a Lenovo tablet set to a phone-sized viewport. These show the development candidate, not a published Play listing.</p><div class="screenshots">'
    for name,label in [('01-home','Home and quick reference'),('02-library','Offline guide library'),('03-guide','Lost outdoors reference guide'),('04-kit','Bug-out bag checklist')]:
        body+=f'<a href="/assets/apps/survival/{name}.png"><img src="/assets/apps/survival/{name}.png" alt="{label}" loading="lazy"></a>'
    body+='</div></section><section><h2>A guide, not a rescue service</h2><p>Survival is informational reference material, not professional medical advice or a guarantee of safety. It is not a medical device and does not diagnose, treat, cure or prevent medical conditions. Consult a qualified healthcare professional for medical decisions.</p><p>The included 1992 Army manual is historical and may contain outdated or dangerous advice. Plant photos cannot establish safe identification or edibility. Maps, GPS readings and facility records may be inaccurate or stale; a listed shelter may be closed. Use training, judgment and backup equipment. Contact local emergency services in an emergency.</p><p>Limited tablet testing has been completed. Independent expert safety review and broader field and Play-installed testing remain pending.</p></section>'+LINKS
    page('/survival/','Survival: Offline Field Guide for Android','Offline guides, regional maps and planning tools for adults. Coming soon: planned $0.99 upfront, no ads or subscriptions.',body,image=image)
    paragraphs=''.join('<p>'+escape(p).replace('\n','<br>')+'</p>' for p in PRIVACY.split('\n\n'))
    page('/survival/privacy/','Survival Privacy Policy','How Survival stores local data and uses optional map and location providers. No app ads, analytics or account.', '<article class="catalog-hero"><h1>Survival privacy policy</h1>'+paragraphs+'<h2>This website</h2><p>The studio website separately offers optional analytics through its consent controls. That website choice does not add analytics to the Survival app.</p>'+LINKS+'</article>',image=image)
    support='<article class="catalog-hero"><h1>Survival support</h1><h2>Read offline</h2><p>Open Library to browse guides or use Home search. Sources &amp; Safety in More contains the persistent safety notice, source links, software licenses and offline privacy policy.</p><h2>Download a map</h2><p>While online, open Navigate → Offline regions. Choose a region, check its size and coverage, then confirm Download. Wi-Fi only is selected by default. Once saved, choose Open offline map. Update and Delete manage that device’s map copy without deleting waypoints.</p><p>Keep enough free space for a replacement download and the existing map. If a provider is unavailable, retry later; already-saved maps remain accessible. Download and check your maps before leaving reception.</p><h2>Location, compass and elevation</h2><p>Allow location only when you want location features. Indoor reception and device sensors affect accuracy. Elevation can be unavailable or inaccurate; the app labels the reference and available accuracy. Straight-line bearings do not identify a safe walking route. Breadcrumb recording stops when Navigate is not visible.</p><h2>Privacy and deletion</h2><p>Online nearby-place refresh asks before sending coordinates to providers. Manual region selection does not need GPS. Delete downloaded regions, waypoints and trails using the app’s controls. Cancel active downloads before clearing app storage. Clearing storage or uninstalling removes local app records; there is no remote app account.</p><h2>Price and availability</h2><p>Planned US$0.99 upfront, for adults 18+, with no ads or in-app purchases. Survival has not been released on Google Play. Purchase and refund support will use Google Play once released.</p><h2>Get help or report a correction</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:tripperdeelabs@gmail.com">tripperdeelabs@gmail.com</a> with the app version, Android version and a non-sensitive description. Do not send precise locations or personal medical details. This inbox is not an emergency service.</p>'+LINKS+'</article>'
    page('/survival/support/','Survival Support','Help with offline maps, guide sources, location tools, local data and Survival release availability.',support,image=image)
